{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "7e3c1a52-9b44-4c2e-8f6a-1d2b3c4e5f60"/*ImageToLaserPoints*/,
  "Description": "Vectorizes a texture into ILDA laser points - the graph-side Find Paths / Find Contours stage that turns rendered images into laser shapes. Bright strokes and edges on a black background become lit laser paths, isolated bright pixels become dwell dots.\n\nFind Paths mode thresholds the image and skeletons it (Zhang-Suen thinning): every thin bright stroke becomes ONE lit centerline - the encoding line art wants. A blob wider than Thickness switches to region outlines (marching squares): a thin line becomes the two-sided ribbon of its edges, matching the Thickness reduction vectorizer guides describe. Find Contours mode runs a Canny edge detector (Gaussian blur, Sobel gradients, non-max suppression, hysteresis) and traces the edges as thin paths - outlines of everything with enough contrast, independent of fill.\n\nThe texture is read back through a staged ring buffer, so the vectorization runs one or two frames behind the rendered image - laser output tolerates this. Downscale uses max-pooling, so a thin bright line survives. Shapes are emitted as blanked approach point + evenly spaced lit samples (the encoding the output pipeline splits into shapes), so the output setup's optimizer (reorder, blanking, corner dwell) and safety stage run on the result unchanged.\n\nLike [LaserCamera] it is laser content: it lists as CONTENT in the Output Setup and routes through its OutputRef; the LaserPoints output feeds [LaserPointsToBuffer] for in-graph preview. The driver's point budget caps the frame; a frame that hits the cap sets the op's status warning.",
  "InputUis": [
    {
      "InputId": "2b7d9c14-6a53-4e91-bc08-3f42d8a95e17"/*UseColor*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 225.0
      },
      "Description": "When on, shapes take the source pixel's color; when off, they are white."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "3f6e1a90-7c2b-4e3d-9a41-5b8c2d7e1f60"/*Texture*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 0.0
      },
      "Description": "Image to vectorize - bright strokes or edges on a black background. Rendered frames, camera feeds and AI outputs all work; the brighter/cleaner the strokes (compression artifacts hurt), the better the result."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "5a8f2d61-9c3b-4e74-bd15-2e7c9a4b1d36"/*MaxPaths*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 450.0
      },
      "Description": "Cap on shapes per frame - the guard against pathological content producing a 3-second frame. Excess shapes are dropped and counted in the stats."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "70ab0278-c054-4175-8025-d73771ef2fd8"/*InFade*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 862.0
      },
      "Description": "Ramps each shape's first samples up from a dim level to full - the scanner is still accelerating when a path starts, which otherwise blooms the start point. 0 = off."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "71b043c3-ae4f-4b33-a48c-93a33ddca3ca"/*OutFade*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 900.0
      },
      "Description": "Ramps the end-repeat samples down, so finishing a shape doesn't leave a bright pause dot of its own. 0 = the repeats hold at full brightness."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "71c3e9a2-8d54-4b16-ae27-9c4f1b2d3e58"/*Denoise*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 375.0
      },
      "Description": "Drop shapes shorter than this many working pixels - kills speckle noise from compressed sources. 0 keeps everything."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "80a65286-1404-437a-b421-baf62a8428c9"/*PathMaxLength*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 1013.0
      },
      "Description": "Drops shapes longer than this percentage of the working image's larger dimension - runaway background strokes. 0 keeps everything."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "8c1e5b39-4a72-4d86-9e20-6b3f7c1a2d45"/*PointSpacing*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 525.0
      },
      "Description": "A point every N working pixels along a shape - laser point distribution along the stroke (like LaserCamera's MaxEdgeStep). Smaller = smoother/brighter lines, more points."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "9d2f4b18-3e57-4c86-b2a9-1f60d3c47e25"/*Mode*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 75.0
      },
      "Description": "Find Paths: threshold + skeleton - one lit centerline per thin stroke (or region outlines for blobs wider than Thickness). Find Contours: Canny edges of the image - outlines of everything with enough contrast."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "a7c1e382-5b94-4d26-8f30-9d1a2b3c4e65"/*OutputRef*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 825.0
      },
      "Description": "Laser output this op feeds - drop the op on an output card in the Output Setup to set it. The driver pulls the frame at pump rate and runs the output's optimizer + safety pipeline."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "b6e2c948-7d13-4a65-8c04-2f1a5b6c7d84"/*Brightness*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 675.0
      },
      "Description": "Global color multiplier (0..1) applied to the emitted points."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "c5e8a273-1b94-4f02-8d36-7a91b4c2e5f8"/*Threshold*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 150.0
      },
      "Description": "Brightness a pixel needs to count as content. Compression noise sits above zero - raise until the background drops out. Canny mode: how strong an edge must be (Sobel magnitude scale)."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "d3b7a164-5e28-4c93-af06-1b9c2d3e4f57"/*MaxRes*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 600.0
      },
      "Description": "Working-resolution cap (256/512/1024/2048). Higher = finer detail, more CPU: 256 is real-time-safe on the laser pump budget; 1024+ is for offline-quality vectorization."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "e4a1b385-2c76-4d02-9f53-8b1c6d2e4a79"/*Thickness*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 300.0
      },
      "Description": "Find Paths only: expected stroke width. 1 = skeletonize everything into centerlines. Higher = blobs wider than this trace as region outlines instead (a thin line then yields the two sides of its ribbon) - matches the Thickness reduction vectorizer guides describe."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "e8f4a261-9c3d-4e57-8b26-4f1a5d3c7e08"/*BlurSize*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 262.0
      },
      "Description": "Find Contours only: Gaussian blur before the Sobel gradient - None or 3/5/7/9 px kernel. Denoises the image so small parts are not detected; the guide's Blur Size."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "f9a4d175-6e32-4b58-9d16-3c8e1b2a4c75"/*Update*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 750.0
      },
      "Description": "Supplier freeze: when off, the last frame keeps streaming and nothing re-vectorizes - the supplier gate every laser content op carries."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "fd3cdd65-3155-4082-880a-ea24bfe5eab9"/*EndRepeat*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 862.0
      },
      "Description": "Extra lit samples held at each shape's end position, so the scanner settles on the real endpoint instead of rounding it off. A dot's dwell time grows with it too - its point intensity."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "ff82f232-0a87-4eba-ae83-e69a803cb2a8"/*PathMinLength*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 975.0
      },
      "Description": "Drops shapes shorter than this percentage of the working image's larger dimension - noise specks that would cost a blank jump each. 0 keeps everything."
    }
  ],
  "SymbolChildUis": [],
  "OutputUis": [
    {
      "OutputId": "c2d4e6f8-a1b2-4c3d-8e4f-5a6b7c8d9e01"/*LaserPoints*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": 300.0,
        "Y": 100.0
      }
    },
    {
      "OutputId": "d5e7f9a1-b3c2-4d4e-9f5a-6b7c8d9e0f12"/*PointCount*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": 300.0,
        "Y": 200.0
      }
    }
  ]
}